+*default_dim_inactive* <value>
+	Sets how much unfocused windows are darkened, as a number from 0.0 to 1.0.
+	A window is unfocused unless its border would be drawn in the
+	*client.focused* colors: it is neither the focused window nor inside the
+	focused container, and a focused workspace contains its tiled windows but
+	not its floating ones. When focus is on an empty workspace, every window is
+	unfocused. An unfocused window is covered across its whole box,
+	the window and its border without the title bar, by its dim color (see
+	*dim_inactive_colors.unfocused* and *dim_inactive_colors.urgent*) at an
+	opacity of _value_ times the alpha of that color. 0.0 darkens nothing.
+	Windows with an amount of their own (see *dim_inactive*) keep it when this
+	changes. The default is 0.0.
+
 *default_floating_border* normal|none|pixel [<n>]
 	Set default border style for new floating windows. This only applies to
 	windows that are spawned in floating mode, not windows that become floating
 	afterwards.
 
+*dim_inactive* <value>
+	Gives the selected windows their own darkening amount while unfocused, as a
+	number from 0.0 to 1.0, instead of the global *default_dim_inactive*. Use it
+	with criteria or in a *for_window* rule. Windows without an amount of their
+	own inherit the global amount, including later changes to it. A window
+	keeps its own amount when the configuration is reloaded.
+
+*dim_inactive_colors.unfocused* <color>
+	Sets the color unfocused windows are darkened with, written as #RRGGBB or
+	#RRGGBBAA. The default is #000000FF.
+
+*dim_inactive_colors.urgent* <color>
+	Sets the color unfocused urgent windows are darkened with, written as
